ege-football/story/_/id/50512475/conference-title-game-clinching-scenarios-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Miami tops Virginia Tech, to face Wake Forest in ACC title game","description":"Miami will play Wake Forest in the ACC title game on Dec. 5 after both teams won on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-22T04:46:52.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50558418/miami-tops-virginia-tech-face-wake-forest-acc-title-game","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079309/xavier-atkins","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xavier_Atkins"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Xavier Atkins","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xavier_Atkins","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:20Z","intro":"Xavier Atkins (born September 12, 2005) is an American college football linebacker. He previously played for the LSU Tigers and Auburn Tigers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Atkins attended Jonesboro-Hodge High School in Jonesboro, Louisiana for three years before transferring to Summer Creek High School in Harris County, Texas for his senior year. As a senior, he had 102 tackles, two sacks and two interceptions. He originally committed to play college football at the University of Missouri before flipping to Louisiana State University (LSU)."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a freshman at LSU in 2024, Atkins played in seven games and had three tackles. After the season, he transferred to Auburn University. He was a starter his first year at Auburn in 2025. Atkins was dismissed from the team after 5 games into the 2026 season."}]}}